# skills/ WAS excluded here, on the theory that SKILL.md prose is asserted line-by-line by skills/backlog/tools/backlog.test.mjs (the groom stamp
# order, the closing "Groomed on disk only" line, the reviewer/execute pair) and would go red on contact. Measured 2026-09-15 rather than assumed: a
# full prettier pass over skills/ left both runners green — 538 skill tests and 1708 jest tests — because every one of those assertions matches a
# substring, not a whole line. The exclusion was protecting against a failure that cannot happen, so it is gone and skills/ is formatted like the rest
# of the tree.
#
# What the measurement DID surface, none of it caught by a test, is the reason to read a skills/ diff more carefully than a server/ one: this is the
# plugin's publish surface, so a cosmetic commit here means push + `pnpm run plugin:sync` and a reship of all six skills for no behaviour change;
# SKILL.md prose is a prompt a model reads rather than documentation a person reads, and the pass rewrote 105 emphasis spans from *word* to _word_,
# which is identical markdown and different tokens; and prettier stripped two trailing blank lines from the orchestrate fixture item below, which is
# exactly the byte class that fixture exists to prove backlog.mjs round-trips. Only that last one is walled off below, because it is the only one a
# rule can catch: the fixture directory holds item files, which are data under test rather than source. Note the ordering it depends on — this entry
# excludes a DIRECTORY, and the `!skills/**/*.md` re-inclusion at the foot of this file cannot reach back inside an excluded directory, so the fixture
# item stays untouched while every other skills/ markdown file is formatted.
skills/*/tools/fixtures/

# Design artifacts: the mockups carry deliberately minified one-line CSS so a screen's whole style block reads at a glance. Prettier would explode each
# of those into hundreds of lines and lose the thing they were drawn for.
docs/superpowers/specs/*.html
docs/superpowers/specs/**/*.html

# Markdown, everywhere except the skills. A repo-wide pass over the 51 tracked .md files outside skills/ changes +3223/-2611 lines and every one of
# those changes is *em* -> _em_ or a table's pipes re-padded — proseWrap: preserve governs prose line breaks only, never emphasis characters, list
# markers or table cells. That is the whole diff: no line gets shorter, nothing gets more readable, and `git blame` on docs/subsystems/invariants.md
# stops pointing at the person who worked out each invariant. The skills are the deliberate exception (see the block above), so they are re-included
# below rather than being left to fall under this rule.
*.md
!skills/**/*.md

# The two stylesheets, byte-pinned the same way client/index.html is, just verified by source-text regex instead of a hash. Three suites read these
# files as TEXT rather than parsing them — test/project-hue.test.ts matches the literal selector `:root,[data-theme="midnight"]` to collect a theme's
# blocks, test/design-guards.test.ts checks §2.2's daylight values and the 11px type floor, and test/run-track-style.test.ts reads the reduced-motion
# and stalled rules. Measured 2026-09-15: a prettier pass turned that selector into `:root,\n[data-theme='midnight']` — a line break and single quotes
# — and took all three suites red, 12 cases in total, for no change to a single rendered pixel. The alternative was loosening three behaviour guards to
# tolerate whitespace, which trades a real check for a cosmetic diff; excluding the files keeps the guards strict and costs nothing.
shared/theme.css
client/src/styles.css
